* Better error reporting (maybe with the anyhow crate): currently,
mato is panicing all over the place.
  DONE: replaced all user-facing unwrap()/panic!()/expect() calls with die!()
  throughout lib.rs, the bins, and process/. The die! macro itself was fixed to
  use $crate:: (so it works inside the library, not only from binaries) and
  wrapped in double braces (so it composes in expression context). anyhow was
  not needed — die! already does the right thing for a CLI tool.

* Improved hyphenation settings: currently, german requires setting explicit
hyphenation codes. These should be introduced automatically, when german
language files are selected.
  DONE: added a hyphenation_setup() function in src/render/groff/mom.rs that
  matches on config.lang and emits .hla / .hpf / .hym 0 / .hy 1 after .START.
  German ("den") loads hyphen.den, English ("en") loads hyphen.en, anything
  else falls back to .hym 0 / .hy 1 only. .hy 1 was kept deliberately to allow
  short 2-char stubs, overriding mom's conservative .hy 14 default.

